body:
Part of #161

Portable, project-agnostic scripts the skill calls:
- check and install Blender's Python module (`bpy`) for the Python version it needs;
- render any `.fbx` / `.glb` / `.blend` from three-quarter, front, side and wireframe (Cycles on CPU, no GPU needed);
- compose a review sheet: concept on the left, renders on the right, a caption with the numbers.

**Done when:** each script runs on a model it has never seen (tested on a PlunderSpell model) and its output has been opened and looked at.

aj's direction (2026-10-15): the guards cause more problems than they prevent. In one session they:
- refused to publish a page, because an earlier permission prompt had gone unanswered, so every later prompt was refused at once ("the page can't be allowed to fail silently and shouldn't be blocked");
- blocked a builder's code edits and a commit while aj was away;
- refused a whole-file rewrite of the agent's own design page;
- stopped a browser check because its output went through `tail`.

## What aj asked for

1. **Remove the "never hide work / blocking background work" prompting** from the rules and the hooks.
2. **Audit every guard** so the only things that block or prompt are genuinely unrecoverable actions, for example:
   - pushing to `main`, or force-pushing to `main`;
   - deleting files that aren't committed;
   - recursive deletes;
   - deleting a branch;
   - anything else that destroys data with no way back.
   Not a minor inconvenience.
3. **A page must never be blocked or fail silently.** Publishing an artifact is never something a guard refuses.

## Plan

An audit page lists every hook that blocks or prompts, with keep / soften to a reminder / drop for each, against the test above. aj approves it, then the changes are built as child issues and one pull request.

Related: the automatic-pages issue (#281) and its children (#282 to #284), whose build is paused until this lands.

Opened by AJ's agent
